A||||122||Cliff Pennock||Make your own PFF T-Shirt!||||4||
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||10-25-2000||02:22 PM||||First off, this is not my idea, credit where credit is due - <B>sdm1964</B> came up with the idea (Check <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004041.html" TARGET=_blank>this</A> thread).<P>I did go ahead and designed a PFF T-Shirt, in fact I'm wearing one right now! It's very easy to make and shouldn't take more than a few minutes. I used that special iron-on inkjet-paper and the result is indistinguishable from a professional printed shirt.<P>For anyone that is interested, I can email you the graphics in any of the following formats: <B>CorelDraw</B> (mention your version number), <B>MS-Word</B>, <B>MS-Works</B> and several other formats.<P>What you need is: Some cheap light-colored or white t-shirts (be prepared to scr3w up your first try), a color printer and special iron-on inkjet-paper (they cost about $10 for 6 sheets here).<P>Follow the instructions of the special paper to the dot (that's how I messed up my first few tries - 'cos I thought I knew better than the instructions) and the results will be great!<P>If you want me to email you the graphics, please reply in this thread (so I know your screen-name). Here's what it will look like:<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumtshirt.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 10-25-2000).]||||reg||4
